"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State precisely what isolates the REAL rebar ticket store during the probe (the remote-less, scrubbed store copy with REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off) rather than crediting REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1, which gates only the MCP write surface the in-process run_python REPL bypasses — keep the flag if desired for defense-in-depth but do not present it as the store-write guarantee.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5067,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1, agent instructed to REPORT not fix'","src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:3 — REBAR_MCP_READONLY gates register_write_tools (MCP surface), and _mcp_reads.py gates reconcile live mode — not an in-process transport","_dc_fixtures.py:189-305 dc_store_copy_repo builds a remote-less repo with REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off — this, not the flag, is what isolates the real store","run_python namespace hands the agent transport / dc.run_bridge / rebar.edit_ticket directly, bypassing MCP"],"finding":"The plan lists REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1 as a guardrail that 'keeps rebar's own ticket store read-only', but the agent's primary tool (run_python) executes an in-process REPL holding a direct JiraDataCenterTransport plus dc.run_bridge and rebar (edit_ticket) — none of which route through the MCP server that REBAR_MCP_READONLY gates. The flag therefore does not constrain what the agent can mutate via its main instrument; the actual isolation of the real ticket store is that the store copy is a scrubbed, remote-less git repo (REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off, no remote), not the readonly flag.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f271d11c931a325bd","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Portability sections and AC line 'sets REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1'","norm_id":"n58ee573d840e89fb","priority":0.2933,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader/implementer trusts REBAR_MCP_READONLY to bound the agent's blast radius when the REPL can mutate freely","The env var is copied forward as the load-bearing safety control in a future reuse of this pattern"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In the Approach/Portability guardrail list, describe the store-write isolation as 'the agent operates only against the ephemeral scrubbed store COPY, which has no git remote and runs with REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=off, so no experiment can reach the real tickets branch'; note REBAR_MCP_READONLY=1 separately as belt-and-suspenders on the MCP surface, not as the primary control.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the minimal RichTextRca contract fields (e.g. hypothesis, experiments[], per-experiment evidence_id + observation, root_cause) and the evidence-id format so AC5's 'cited experiment evidence' is verifiable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7389,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Returns a structured RichTextRca finding, each experiment cited to evidence ids.'","AC5: 'uploads a RichTextRca finding with cited experiment evidence'","No field list, evidence-id format, or root-cause field is stated"],"finding":"The RichTextRca finding contract is named as a 'registered structured contract' but its fields/shape and the shape of the per-experiment 'evidence ids' it cites are never specified, leaving the executor to invent them.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc067019a69412c74","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach (new test file bullet) + AC3/AC5","norm_id":"ncdac54082dc7a1fc","priority":0.0611,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must guess whether RichTextRca carries root_cause, hypothesis, experiments[], evidence_ids, reproduction status, etc.","AC5's 'cited experiment evidence' cannot be checked without knowing the evidence-id shape"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a short contract sketch to the Approach section listing RichTextRca's required fields and the shape of each experiment's evidence id.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_jus