"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add an AC bounding the agent (max turns / wall-clock budget), a job-level timeout in the workflow, and require the finding+evidence artifact to upload even on agent error (with the error captured), so failures are observable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Define the RichTextRca contract's fields in the plan, and explicitly enumerate the closed value vocabulary of any categorisation field (e.g. failing_layer: store_read | codec | differ | transport | seed | cutover_config | other) the agent must emit.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7511,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'Returns a structured `RichTextRca` finding, each experiment cited to evidence ids.'","AC3: 'returns a registered structured `RichTextRca` contract'","The plan never enumerates the contract's fields or the value space of any closed-vocabulary field the agent must fill.","Grounding that such an enum is load-bearing: the existing implementation defines failing_layer with a fixed vocabulary 'store_read | codec | differ | transport | seed | cutover_config | other' in tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_richtext_agentic_probe.py — a closed enum the agent must emit exactly.","The analogous capability-map contract likewise pins a closed 'present | absent | present_but_different' verdict vocabulary (scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py), showing this pattern relies on stated enums."],"finding":"The plan names an LLM-emitted structured-output contract 'RichTextRca' but never defines its field/enum value vocabulary — in particular any closed-vocabulary categorisation field the agent must emit exactly (the implemented sibling contract constrains failing_layer to 'store_read | codec | differ | transport | seed | cutover_config | other', a vocabulary nowhere stated in the plan).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3d375f2c212714c7","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('Returns a structured RichTextRca finding') and AC3 ('returns a registered structured RichTextRca contract')","norm_id":"n6e383b1472ea4fc8","priority":0.0489,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer or the agent has no plan-level definition of the RichTextRca failing-layer categories, so the emitted categorisation is free-form and not comparable across runs.","A reviewer cannot confirm the contract captures the mechanism→layer attribution the ticket needs because the layer vocabulary is unspecified."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add to the Approach/AC a one-line schema sketch for RichTextRca listing its fields and, for failing_layer (or equivalent), the exact allowed enum values the agent must choose from.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","eviden